  "text": "The seed is in the prepared spot. Cover it with Grandma.\n\nA strip of sticky material used to hold things together.\n\nA thing already mentioned, or something belonging to it.\n\nBelieved something without checking whether it was true.\n\nShows a direction, recipient, or an action that follows.\n\nA round, open container used for mixing or holding food.\n\nIntroduces possibilities or a question about something.\n\nSay that a choice or arrangement is the one you intend.\n\nM7 7V5a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v2M5 7h14l1 14H4L5 7Zm3 6h8v5H8v-5\n\nKnew something because you had heard or seen it before.\n\nMara needs the footbridge secured before she can cross.\n\nRead your ending aloud as Sol. Pause at each full stop.\n\nThe person speaking; my means belonging to that person.\n\nUnits of time; here they are the times when Mara works.\n\nLine up the torn wing, then place tape across the tear.\n\nA polite word used when asking someone to do something.\n\nMara’s lantern shows the boy holding his sister’s bird.\n\nLooked closely to find out whether something was right.\n\nDescribes something that is a good idea or is expected.\n\nA piece of woven material; a tablecloth covers a table.\n\nLets other people hear, use or take part in something.\n\nHow would starting later help me get to the gathering?\n\nAny longer; used when something has stopped happening.\n\nAll the passengers are ashore. Mara has finished work.\n\nChoose a word if you would like help with its meaning.\n\nShows something necessary for the condition described.\n\nPip gives Grandma’s written story to Mara at her dock.\n\nMore than is possible or wanted; sometimes means also.\n\nThe footbridge is secure. Guide Pip across to Grandma.\n\nAt Mara’s dock · Hear her reply to the delivered story\n\nThe boy holds the paper bird he promised to keep safe.",
  "textSha256": "d807e9cbefe9aed4f8756613fe7e9d4f679f439f9c1def632519d5ba2295de47",
